  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> is the set of distinct values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> for which the following system of linear equations<br /><br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br />has no solution, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp; is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WPWzi",
      "text": "An empty set",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FJuHL",
      "text": "An infinite set",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "naXdI",
      "text": "A finite set containing two or more elements",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FCcm3",
      "text": "A singleton",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For no solution&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Expanding the determinant along the first row, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>For&nbsp;<math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, first two planes are coincident.</p><p>Now, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>For no solution, these two planes are parallel.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;&#8658;&#160;</mo></math>it is a singleton set</p>",
    "image": null
  },
